            <title>[LU-13459] sanity-lfsck test_10: lfsck does not complete before 32s timeout</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13459</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Olaf Faaland &amp;lt;faaland1@llnl.gov&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/ab082c06-d3f6-4bdf-8275-f5a14b216edf" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/ab082c06-d3f6-4bdf-8275-f5a14b216edf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_10 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;(16) unexpected status
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Occurred testing a patch based on b2_12.  This was the only failure in a standard test run (ie no Test-Parameters specified).  There were 2 clients, 4 MDTs, and 8 OSTs.  5 VMs total.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test has run a "namespace" type lfsck and is waiting for it to finish.&lt;br/&gt;
This is done via wait_update_facet() checking the output of get_param -n mdd.${MDT_DEV}.lfsck_namespace for '^status:.*completed".  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;wait_update_facet() reported "Update not seen after 32s: wanted 'completed' got 'scanning-phase2'"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are no console log warnings or errors during the test run, on any of the nodes.&lt;/p&gt;







&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanity-lfsck test_10 - (16) unexpected status&lt;/p&gt;</description>
